sched: keep the critmon CPU load in perf counts, skip a NULL outgoing task

Purpose: with SCHED_CPULOAD_CRITMONITOR, nxsched_switch_critmon() and
nxsched_update_critmon() convert each run of a task to system ticks
(elapsed * CLOCKS_PER_SEC / perf_getfreq()) before adding it to the CPU
load.  The division rounds down, so every run shorter than a tick (100 us
here, CONFIG_USEC_PER_TICK) adds nothing and every longer run loses its
remainder: tasks that run often and briefly (the IMU threads, the NINA
event thread, interrupt-woken threads) are under-counted and the idle task
over-counted.  It is also a 64-bit division at every context switch, which
the Cortex-M0+ does in software.

- sched_critmonitor.c: add the elapsed perf counts as they are.
- sched_critmonitor.c: return at once when the outgoing task is NULL.  On
  the ARMv6-M, up_exit() (arch/arm/src/common/arm_exit.c) sets
  g_running_tasks[] to NULL before the last switch away from an exiting
  task, and arm_doirq() (arch/arm/src/armv6-m/arm_doirq.c) then calls
  nxsched_switch_context(NULL, tcb).  nxsched_switch_critmon() read
  run_start through the NULL pointer (on the RP2040, the boot ROM at
  address 0) and added the difference to g_cpuload_total: the total went
  negative, was never scaled back, and every load read 0.0 %.  The
  exiting task's time was already accounted when nxtask_exit() switched
  away from it, before its TCB was released, and to->run_start was set
  then.
- sched_cpuload.c: with SCHED_CPULOAD_CRITMONITOR, count the time constant
  (SCHED_CPULOAD_TIMECONSTANT seconds) in perf counts, perf_getfreq() per
  second.

Only ratios of the counts are read (clock_cpuload(): /proc/cpuload,
/proc/<pid>/loadavg, the CPU column of ps, the task list of a PANIC
report), so their meaning does not change.  The board's perf counter is the
1 MHz TIMER (boards/arduino-nano-rp2040-connect/src/nano_perf.c); the
counts of a 2-second time constant fit easily in clock_t (64 bits).
Zephyr: the Zephyr build's thread usage (CONFIG_SCHED_THREAD_USAGE) adds
the cycles of each run without rounding.

diff --git a/sched/sched/sched_cpuload.c b/sched/sched/sched_cpuload.c
index 3eb62043..bba533a6 100644
--- a/sched/sched/sched_cpuload.c
+++ b/sched/sched/sched_cpuload.c
@@ -48,6 +48,10 @@
 #    error CONFIG_SCHED_CPULOAD_TICKSPERSEC is not defined
 #  endif
 #  define CPULOAD_TICKSPERSEC CONFIG_SCHED_CPULOAD_TICKSPERSEC
+#elif defined(CONFIG_SCHED_CPULOAD_CRITMONITOR)
+/* sched_critmonitor.c accounts the load in perf counts. */
+
+#  define CPULOAD_TICKSPERSEC ((clock_t)perf_getfreq())
 #else
 #  define CPULOAD_TICKSPERSEC CLOCKS_PER_SEC
 #endif
diff --git a/sched/sched/sched_critmonitor.c b/sched/sched/sched_critmonitor.c
index 7e12f367..0e302558 100644
--- a/sched/sched/sched_critmonitor.c
+++ b/sched/sched/sched_critmonitor.c
@@ -370,13 +370,30 @@ void nxsched_critmon_busywait(bool state, FAR void *caller)
 
 void nxsched_switch_critmon(FAR struct tcb_s *from, FAR struct tcb_s *to)
 {
-  clock_t current = perf_gettime();
-  clock_t elapsed = current - from->run_start;
+  clock_t current;
+  clock_t elapsed;
+
+  /* On the ARMv6-M, up_exit() clears g_running_tasks[] before the switch
+   * away from an exiting task, so arm_doirq() passes from == NULL.  That
+   * task's time was accounted when nxtask_exit() switched away from it
+   * (before its TCB was released), and to->run_start was set then.
+   */
+
+  if (from == NULL)
+    {
+      return;
+    }
+
+  current = perf_gettime();
+  elapsed = current - from->run_start;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_CPULOAD_CRITMONITOR
-  clock_t tick = elapsed * CLOCKS_PER_SEC / perf_getfreq();
+  /* The load is kept in perf counts (CPULOAD_TICKSPERSEC in
+   * sched_cpuload.c): converting each run to system ticks here would
+   * round every run shorter than a tick down to nothing.
+   */
 
-  nxsched_critmon_cpuload(from, current, tick);
+  nxsched_critmon_cpuload(from, current, elapsed);
 #endif
 
 #if CONFIG_SCHED_CRITMONITOR_MAXTIME_THREAD >= 0
@@ -465,9 +482,7 @@ void nxsched_update_critmon(FAR struct tcb_s *tcb)
   if (tcb->task_state == TSTATE_TASK_RUNNING)
     {
 #ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_CPULOAD_CRITMONITOR
-      clock_t tick = elapsed * CLOCKS_PER_SEC / perf_getfreq();
-
-      nxsched_process_taskload_ticks(tcb, tick);
+      nxsched_process_taskload_ticks(tcb, elapsed);
 #endif
 
       tcb->run_start = current;
